Knowing the age of a mobile phone is of great importance, since that way you can know if it still has the valid warranty. For that reason, if you notice that your phone has started to fail, has become slower than normal, or is freezing, you should verify the date you purchased it.
But if when checking the purchase date, you realize that the warranty is still valid, you can take it directly to the store where you bought it or take it to the manufacturer. This is important for you to consider, because remember that when buying a mobile you usually they offer two guarantees.
The location of this date usually varies, since it will depend on the type of voucher that you have been given. In this case, if you were given a purchase receipt, the date will be at the bottom of it.
It will only be a matter of verifying which voucher model is the one you have so that you can know the exact date of purchase. Taking into account this information and the one you read in the previous point, you can realize the importance of saving the invoices that are given to you when making a purchase.
However, if you can't find it, you can also make a request to the seller for a certified copy of the original invoice. It is a procedure that may take time, but it will undoubtedly help you to know the age of a mobile.
