Modern Windows 10 computers keep a particular chunk of Internet connection bandwidth aside and use it for certain live applications. They contain 20% of the full bandwidth, but you can configure it according to your needs and QoS Packet Schedulerhelps in this regard.
QoS is a feature for traffic allocation in Windows and its full form is Quality of Service. When a network uses this, it gives an administrator the ability to prioritize one defined network traffic over a different one.
QoS Packet Scheduler in Windows 10 is a kind of network bandwidth management method that monitors the importance of data packets. This depends on the priority of the packet and provides lower or higher priority or bandwidth tiers to the connection.
The QoS Packet Scheduler only affects LAN traffic and not Internet access speeds. For it to work, it must be supported on each side of the connection.
