How can I tell if the Windows Time service is working?
The Windows Time service is a Microsoft service that provides clock synchronization for the Windows operating system. If your device is displaying the wrong time and you are sure it is not a time zone issue, you may want to make sure that the Windows time service is working properly before applying any fixes.
