1 How can I control the speed of my CPU fan in Windows 10?
An essential part of a PC setup, small but remarkably robust. However, if it is exposed to abnormal temperatures for an extended period of time (we gamers, we're looking at it), the CPU could fail.
Now, there are several ways around that (extra cooling fans are probably the best), and today we are going to show you one that is quite important - how to increase CPU fan speed.
How can I control the speed of my CPU fan in Windows 10?
There are a few conditions you will need to meet in order to use it, and the setup isn't exactly a walk in the park, but once you get your hands on it, SpeedFan will become an indispensable part of your daily workflow.
As for CPU and GPU fanatics, you should be able to control them without any problem. Laptops are an exception, and SpeedFan will be of no use with laptops except for monitoring
There, you can choose the percentage of fan speed (100% is the maximum throttle). On the right side, you should see the current temperatures of the individual CPU cores.
Your CPU speed should never cross 70 degrees Celsius, and around 60 degrees is an acceptable limit for the extended period of time.
