2 How to find a person's IP address
To do this, we will explain how you can obtain it by email. In addition, you will learn what you must do to have the geographical location of a person once you have obtained their IP.
Therefore, the IP could be compared with the identity document of a person or the license plate of a car, since each of them is unique and its objective is to identify them. Additionally, just as people must use their identity document to carry out any procedure, in the same way each device that connects to the Internet must have an address to be able to communicate.
Therefore, it must be taken into account that there are two types of IP, on the one hand, there is the public one, which are the ones that identify and locate the devices connected to the Internet. On the other hand, there is the local IP address that, as its name indicates, identifies the IPs connected to a local network, such as modems, routers, among others.
This considering that all the technical details of the email appear in its header, obviously including the IP address. However, this is not information that you will find just by opening the email.
Once the email opens, click on the "Properties" option located at the top of the screen.
Then you are going to select "Details".
In this way, all the details of the received email will appear, including what you are looking for, the sender's IP address.
If the web service you use to manage your emails is Apple Mail, you must follow the following steps to know the IP of the person who writes to you:
When entering, search and select the email of whom you want to know the IP.
