Your organization has disabled automatic updates for Windows 10 - A considerable number of users as soon as they met Microsoft are hiding data, instantly browsing the Internet and implementing the recommended modifications on various reputable sites. The suggestions were about blocking the Update and the changes were made through the Registry Editor and Group Policy Editor, thus unknowingly manipulating the Settings in question.
The note institutedjust for your organization has disabled automatic updates just below the "Choose how updates are installed" drop-down menu indicates that you have set the priority through the Group Policy Editor on your own. When you go to Settings => Update & Security => Windows update => Advanced options you draw that under the first block, a drop-down menu designated Never Check for Updates (Not recommended) is determined and displayed in gray.
Open Group Policy Editor using its favorable method. If you don't know either way, then jointly press the "Win andR" keys and type "gpedit.msc" and click "Enter."
Computer Configuration => Administrative Template => Windows Component => Windows Update => Configure Automatic Update
>> Locate the checkboxes of the 3 round cells at the top of the settings and check “Enabled”.
