Having a good and reliable VPN is important, and in today's article, we will show you how to connect your PC to a VPN in Windows 10.
Whether for business or personal use, a VPN or virtual private network gives you a more secure connection to your network and the Internet, as if you were working from a public place.
How to connect to a VPN in Windows 10?
Create a VPN profile on your laptop in Windows 10
Go to Connection name and enter any name, for example My personal VPN for the VPN connection profile. This is the same name that you will look for when you want to connect in the server name, or in the address box.
En VPN type , select the type of VPN connection you want to create. This means that you need to know what type of VPN service your company uses.
Now that you have created a VPN profile for a work account or for personal use, you are ready to connect to a VPN.
Go to the right side of the taskbar.
Select the VPN connection you want to use.
Once you are connected, you will see the name of the VPN connection with the word Connected underneath. If you want to see if you are connected, select the Network icon and then check if the VPN connection shows the word Connected below it.
If the above methods seem a bit complicated, you can also connect to a VPN using a third-party VPN client. This method is the simplest, and to be able to use it, you just need to download and install a VPN client and log in to it.
If you're looking for a good VPN client, be sure to check out our review of the best VPN clients for Windows 10.
