Due to the increase in a number of cases where employees use their own devices within their company, the cases of accidental data leaks through their applications and services have also increased.
To help resolve these issues, Windows developers released Windows Information Protection (WIP). This service helps you protect your business data and applications from accidental leaks.
WIP is the MAM (mobile application management) system for Windows 10. This handy tool offers you the ability to manage all aspects of data policy enforcement for both applications and documents.
If this option is chosen, WIP automatically encrypts and stores the data locally, so that the company administrator can access it easily and securely. The company administrator can configure personalized access to applications and other restrictions, and also keep a record of all changes made to the system.
