Researchers found that women are much less likely than men to get a good night’s sleep when there are children at home. They say this can explain why some women feel so tired compared to others.
For the purpose of the study, the researchers surveyed more than 5,800 people and asked them how long they slept last month and how tired they felt. Participants analyzed factors such as age, race, education level, marital status, number of children in the family, income, body mass index, exercise, employment, and hitting to assess any link to sleep deprivation.
In addition, the researchers found that 62% of women in this group without children can sleep at least seven hours a night. For women with children, this figure drops to 48%.
