The electric bike federal tax credit, similar to the electric vehicle tax credit, has been the big news this year since it was first proposed in February.
House of as part of the Build Back Better Act. The tax credit is capped at $900, down from the original planned $15,000 limit.It only works with e-bikes under $4,000.The original plan limited the tax credit to e-bikes priced under $8,000.The lower bound rules out some of the more expensive e-bike options that come with price tags tied to their ability to spend years replacing their daily commuter cars.
The inclusion of e-bikes in the federal tax credit follows extensive support and lobbying from the public and groups such as PeopleForBikes.
