Reduce, Reuse, and Recycle: The “Big Three” of sustainable living. Everyone knows the phrase, but not everyone knows the environmental benefits of recycled paper.
For every 2,000 pounds of recycled paper, 17 trees, 380 gallons of oil, and 7,000 gallons of water are conserved. Natural resource conservation is essential for our planet’s current and long-term health.
Saving just 17 trees can significantly impact the carbon dioxide levels in the air. Seventeen trees can absorb 250 pounds of carbon dioxide, reducing greenhouse gas emissions.
