Over 300 Factories Shut Down As TOTO Employees In Vietnam Confirmed
According to the Hanoi Labour Federation, new cases of infection have continued to emerge in Vietnam’s industrial zones in Hanoi over the past week and a number of companies, including TOTO, have been affected.
According to the 45 local direct grassroots trade unions, there are now a large number of trade union members and workers from F0 to F4 especially affected by the Covid-19 epidemic. To date, 330 enterprises in Hanoi are out of business (40 more than the previous week).
In line with the local government policy, Caesar Vietnam has temporarily reduced some of its production capacity during this period.
