Record low Kenyan Shilling may find support The Shilling slipped to a fresh record low against the dollar this week, trading at 113.35/113.95 compared to 113.30/113.90 at last week’s close as broad demand for the greenback outstripped supply from remittances and exports.
Given that the country’s FX reserves remain adequate at just under $8.8bn—sufficient for 5.36 months of import cover—we expect the Shilling to find some support at current levels in the near term.
