The Managing Director of Republic Bank (Ghana) PLC, Farid Antar has been recognized as the CEO of the Year 2021 – Private Bank Category in Ghana.
The award is in recognition of his outstanding contribution to the financial services sector of Ghana over the past three years.
Speaking on the award, Mr Farid Antar thanked the Award organizers for the special recognition and dedicated the Award to the Executives and Staff of Republic Bank.
According to Mr. Antar, he takes pride in the progress and achievements of the Bank over the last three years and the significant contribution by each staff.
Recounting major milestones of the Bank over the last three years, the Managing Director of Republic Bank said the Bank has been full of activities for the past three years, retooling and innovating for superior banking convenience and experience for Customers. “We have given many of our banking halls major facelifts including the construction of the Republic Court situated at the prestigious Ridge Roundabout enclave.
The Bank also supported various health centres in the fight by donating a cumulative sum of GHS1.2 million. Recently, Republic Bank announced two new innovative mortgage repayment options, also the first of its kind to save customers and prospects up to 40% of their mortgage interest cost, thus allowing them to make an early repayment, Mr Antar added.
